To make the circle element in this code snippet look more 3D, you can follow these steps:

1. Add depth to the circle by changing its background color to a linear gradient with two colors. Here's an example:

   ```css
   .circle {
     fill: radial-gradient(white, lightblue); /* Existing line */
     background: linear-gradient(to bottom, #fff, #ffcccc); /* New line */
   }
   ```

   This will add a subtle highlight effect to the circle when it's rotated or moved around.

2. Add a drop shadow effect to the circle using the `filter` property. Here's how to do it:

   ```css
   .circle {
     filter: drop-shadow(15px 15px 15px gray); /* New line */
   }
   ```

   You can adjust the values of the drop shadow (e.g., the blur radius and color) to suit your needs.

3. To make the circle appear more rounded, increase the value of the `border-radius` property. Here's how to do it:

   ```css
